{
  "_comment": "OPS-LANDING-AUTO-ALIGN-W1 (2026-05-25) snapshot manifest. Architect-ratified at Plan-Mode R1. Defines per-claim find/replace rules applied to landing/*.html on every Hetzner deploy. Script: scripts/snapshot-landing-data.mjs. Adding a new claim = manifest row, no code change.",
  "sot_endpoints": {
    "performance": "https://api.algovault.com/api/performance-public",
    "merkle": "https://api.algovault.com/api/merkle-batches"
  },
  "fetch_timeout_ms": 10000,
  "log_path": "/var/log/algovault-snapshot-landing.log",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "dtrf-call-count",
      "find_pattern": "(data-tr-field=\"call_count\"[^>]*>)[^<]+(<)",
      "replace_template": "$1{value}$2",
      "sot": "performance",
      "accessor": "totalCalls",
      "format": "integer_with_commas",
      "apply_to_files": [
        "landing/index.html",
        "landing/how-it-works.html",
        "landing/skills.html"
      ],
      "replace_all": true
    },
    {
      "id": "dtrf-exchange-count",
      "find_pattern": "(data-tr-field=\"exchange_count\"[^>]*>)[^<]+(<)",
      "replace_template": "$1{value}$2",
      "sot": "performance",
      "accessor": "exchange_count",
      "format": "integer",
      "apply_to_files": [
        "landing/index.html",
        "landing/how-it-works.html",
        "landing/skills.html",
        "landing/faq.html"
      ],
      "replace_all": true
    },
    {
      "_comment": "OPS-LANDING-FUNDING-VENUE-RECONCILE-W1: funding-arb venue-count span (=7), single-derived from FUNDING_VENUE_COUNT via /api/performance-public.funding_venue_count. Mirrors dtrf-exchange-count.",
      "id": "dtrf-funding-venue-count",
      "find_pattern": "(data-tr-field=\"funding_venue_count\"[^>]*>)[^<]+(<)",
      "replace_template": "$1{value}$2",
      "sot": "performance",
      "accessor": "funding_venue_count",
      "format": "integer",
      "apply_to_files": [
        "landing/faq.html"
      ],
      "replace_all": true
    },
    {
      "_comment": "OPS-LANDING-FUNDING-VENUE-RECONCILE-W1: general perp venue count in ld+json / free-text descriptions ('N crypto perp venues') → keeps the digit synced to exchange_count. Venue-count substring ONLY; does NOT match data-tr-field spans ('12</span> crypto perp venues' is non-contiguous) and does NOT touch docs.html (DOCS-GENERATOR domain).",
      "id": "jsonld-perp-venue-count",
      "find_pattern": "\\d+( crypto perp venues)",
      "replace_template": "{value}$1",
      "sot": "performance",
      "accessor": "exchange_count",
      "format": "integer",
      "apply_to_files": [
        "landing/index.html",
        "landing/faq.html",
        "landing/glossary.html"
      ],
      "replace_all": true
    },
    {
      "_comment": "OPS-LANDING-FUNDING-VENUE-RECONCILE-W1: general perp count in free-text 'N exchanges' prose/meta descriptions → exchange_count. On landing surfaces 'N exchanges' is always the venue count; data-tr-field spans are non-contiguous ('12</span> exchanges') so they are untouched.",
      "id": "text-perp-exchange-count",
      "find_pattern": "\\d+( exchanges)",
      "replace_template": "{value}$1",
      "sot": "performance",
      "accessor": "exchange_count",
      "format": "integer",
      "apply_to_files": [
        "landing/index.html"
      ],
      "replace_all": true
    },
    {
      "_comment": "OPS-LANDING-FUNDING-VENUE-RECONCILE-W1: index.html eyebrow 'N venues unified behind one MCP' → exchange_count.",
      "id": "eyebrow-venues-unified",
      "find_pattern": "\\d+( venues unified behind one MCP)",
      "replace_template": "{value}$1",
      "sot": "performance",
      "accessor": "exchange_count",
      "format": "integer",
      "apply_to_files": [
        "landing/index.html"
      ],
      "replace_all": true
    },
    {
      "id": "dtrf-hold-rate",
      "find_pattern": "(data-tr-field=\"hold_rate\"[^>]*>)[^<]+(<)",
      "replace_template": "$1{value}%$2",
      "sot": "performance",
      "accessor": "hold_rate",
      "format": "float_1dp",
      "_note": "NOT monotonic — a HOLD rate can fall, so this is never FLOOR-coerced. The replace_template writes the % INSIDE the span, which is the contract every span must match: a span holding a bare number FOLLOWED by a literal % bakes into '99.2%%'. That shipped to the npm README twice (91.6%%, 99.1%%) and was 'fixed' both times by deleting the inner % — the wrong side, which re-arms on the next inject. Guarded by scripts/check-live-numeric-claims.mjs (OPS-DOCS-HOLDRATE-LIVE-W1). Partials added by OPS-JSONLD-PFE-PROPERTYVALUE-MANAGE-W1: landing/docs.html is GENERATED from docs-src/partials/*, so injecting only the generated page leaves the generator's input stale and the next build_docs re-emits the old value. Inject the source AND the output, or neither holds.",
      "apply_to_files": [
        "README.md",
        "docs-src/partials/faq.html",
        "docs-src/partials/pricing.html",
        "landing/docs.html",
        "landing/faq.html",
        "landing/glossary.html",
        "landing/index.html"
      ],
      "replace_all": true
    },
    {
      "id": "dtrf-merkle-batch-count",
      "find_pattern": "(data-tr-field=\"merkle_batch_count\"[^>]*>)[^<]+(<)",
      "replace_template": "$1{value}$2",
      "sot": "merkle",
      "accessor": "batch_count",
      "format": "integer",
      "apply_to_files": [
        "landing/index.html",
        "landing/how-it-works.html"
      ],
      "replace_all": true
    },
    {
      "id": "dtrf-batch-count",
      "find_pattern": "(data-tr-field=\"batch_count\"[^>]*>)[^<]+(<)",
      "replace_template": "$1{value}$2",
      "sot": "merkle",
      "accessor": "batch_count",
      "format": "integer",
