    {
      "id": "jsonld-propertyvalue-pfe-wr",
      "find_pattern": "(\"name\": \"PFE win rate\", \"value\": \")\\d+\\.\\d(%\")",
      "replace_template": "$1{value}$2",
      "sot": "performance",
      "accessor": "overall.pfeWinRate*100",
      "format": "float_1dp",
      "_note": "The schema.org additionalProperty/PropertyValue form. It inverts the order the older jsonld-description-pfe-rate matches (that one needs the % to PRECEDE the label; here it follows), so it escaped management entirely and rotted to 91.8% against a live 91.7%. A crawler runs no JS, so unlike a data-tr-field span this can never self-heal — it is only ever as fresh as the last deploy-time injection. Same accessor as every other PFE claim on purpose: one fact, one SoT path. Third instance of 'a new phrasing escapes a phrasing-specific regex', which is why OPS-JSONLD-PFE-PROPERTYVALUE-MANAGE-W1 also shipped scripts/check-claim-coverage.mjs to invert match -> coverage.",
      "apply_to_files": [
        "docs-src/template.html",
        "landing/docs.html",
        "landing/faq.html",
        "landing/glossary.html",
        "landing/how-it-works.html",
        "landing/index.html",
        "landing/integrations.html",
        "landing/privacy.html",
        "landing/skills.html",
        "landing/terms.html",
        "landing/tools.html",
        "landing/verify.html"
      ],
      "replace_all": true
    },
    {
      "id": "jsonld-faq-pfe-win-rate-is",
      "find_pattern": "(win rate is )\\d+\\.\\d(% on a rolling)",
      "replace_template": "$1{value}$2",
      "sot": "performance",
      "accessor": "overall.pfeWinRate*100",
      "format": "float_1dp",
      "_note": "FOURTH phrasing of the same fact, found by this wave's own coverage sweep: the FAQPage JSON-LD Answer text says 'win rate is N.N% on a rolling 30-day window'. Percent FOLLOWS the number and the label PRECEDES it, so neither jsonld-description-pfe-rate nor the PropertyValue row matches. It was stale at 90.2 against a live 91.7. Crawler-facing and JS-free, so it can never self-heal.",
      "apply_to_files": [
        "landing/faq.html"
      ],
      "replace_all": true
    },
    {
      "id": "jsonld-skills-pfe-wr-merkle-verified",
